787:In this section we shall look at the monochromatic circumference of a graph. We begin by proving Theorem \ref{Thm: circumference}.
788:\begin{proof}[Proof of Theorem \ref{Thm: circumference}]
791:\item There is a component of $R_{H}$ or $B_{H}$ which contains a matching on at least $\left( \frac{2}{3} +\delta \right)k$ vertices.
796:In the first case, we use the Blow-Up Lemma as in Theorem \ref{Thm: main result} to find a monochromatic cycle of length at least $\left(\frac{2}{3}+\frac{\delta}{2}\right)n$. In the second case, assume without loss of generality that $\Delta(R_{H}[S]) \leq 10\delta k$. Then, by Lemma \ref{Lemma: large sparse set}, $G$ contains a blue cycle of length $\ell$ for all $\ell \in \left[3,\left(\frac{2}{3}-\delta\right)n\right]$. In the third case \ref{Lemma: pathological case} implies that $G$ contains a monochromatic cycle of length at least $\left(1-59\delta\right)n \geq \left(\frac{2}{3}+\delta\right)n$.
