The paper’s main theorem is existential: dense 2-coloured graphs contain prescribed monochromatic cycles except for one classified extremal family. The obvious witness is indeed a vertex cycle, but this does not establish a hard generated distribution. I’m now checking whether the paper’s extremal constructions offer an honest Track B gap before rejecting the planted-cycle idea.
